{#
  Renders a LAVA job metadata block.

  The including template sets METADATA to the named keys it wants to emit.
  Those are the stable vocabulary: a query written against one of them means
  the same thing whichever project rendered the job, so they are always
  emitted, empty when unset.

  EXTRA_METADATA carries anything else a caller wants to record without
  needing a change here. It is a mapping, so in an ini variables file it is a
  section and in a YAML one a nested key:

    [EXTRA_METADATA]              EXTRA_METADATA:
    kernel-recipe = "linux-qcom"    kernel-recipe: linux-qcom

  A key that collides with a named one is dropped rather than emitted twice:
  the named value wins, because it is the one queries are written against,
  and a duplicate key would fail the whole job.

  Values are rendered with tojson so that a value YAML would otherwise read as
  something else - a branch called "yes", a sha that is all digits - stays the
  string it was.
#}
{%- for key, value in METADATA.items() %}
  {{ key }}: {{ value | tojson }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for key, value in (EXTRA_METADATA | default({})).items() if key not in METADATA %}
  {{ key }}: {{ value | tojson }}
{%- endfor %}
